---
import OptimizedImage from "@/components/optimizedImage.astro";
---

<section id="about" class="relative overflow-hidden bg-neutral-50 text-neutral-900 dark:bg-neutral-950 dark:text-neutral-100">
  <div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 -z-10 bg-[radial-gradient(60%_40%_at_50%_0%,rgba(255,255,255,.06),transparent)]"></div>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-24 sm:py-32">
    <div class="relative">
      <div
        aria-hidden="true"
        class="pointer-events-none absolute right-0 -top-10 select-none text-right font-black leading-[0.78] tracking-tighter text-neutral-900/5 dark:text-neutral-100/5"
      >
        <span class="block text-[18vw]">Developer</span>
        <span class="block -mt-3 text-[18vw]">Designer</span>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 items-start gap-8 sm:gap-12 lg:grid-cols-12">
        <div class="lg:col-span-5">
          <figure class="overflow-hidden rounded-2xl shadow-2xl">
            <OptimizedImage
              src={import("../../public/photos/IMGA0704_3.webp")}
              alt="Portrait of Nestor Kulik"
              class="h-auto w-full object-contain grayscale"
            />
          </figure>
        </div>
        <div class="lg:col-span-7">
          <p class="max-w-2xl text-2xl font-medium leading-tight tracking-tight text-neutral-800 dark:text-neutral-200 sm:text-3xl lg:text-4xl">
            I like products that feel composed from the first click: clear structure, quiet confidence, and details that
            hold up under real use.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-12 grid max-w-2xl grid-cols-1 gap-6 md:grid-cols-5">
            <div class="col-span-1 text-sm tracking-widest text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-300 md:col-span-2">
              <span class="font-mono">( ABOUT ME )</span>
            </div>
            <div class="col-span-2 leading-normal text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300 md:col-span-3">
              My work sits where UX structure, frontend craft, and visual judgment overlap. I care about information
              architecture, accessible interfaces, restrained motion, and systems that make teams faster instead of
              noisier. Outside of product work I photograph cities, skies, and quiet details, build side projects, and
              spend a lot of time looking for better ways to make digital things feel intentional.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
